{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/461175-male-uratha-pregnancy","id":461175,"title":"Male Uratha Pregnancy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-29T10:25:07-07:00","id":461175,"title":"Male Uratha Pregnancy","content":"So in 2ed corebook we have little sidebar about male characters becoming &quot;mothers&quot; with Gifts like <i>Luna's Embrace</i>. I'm very interested in this transgender subject, as myself non-heteronomative male, I ask: How can this be done? Does <i>Luna's Embrace</i> is needed to change male character in to female on all the time of pregnancy? So if character would return to his original sex, he would lost the child?<br /> <br /> If not, does the child is spiritual with his parents other gender form, like items are &quot;dedicated&quot; to you when you are in inhuman forms? If that's the case, does Harmony have the same repercussions?<br /> <br /> I see very interesting story idea in the subject here... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T11:42:28-07:00","id":461277,"title":"","content":"The phrasing of Luna's Embrace does seem to indicate that you'd have to stay in a female body the whole time. Switching biological sex via the Gift is noted as complete switching. Going from female to male means loosing a functional uterus. If you wanted to bend things a bit with some science (and not just wave things away with magic), <b>very</b> early on, a human male body does have a small cluster of cells that never form into a functional female reproductive system and there's no inherent reason a zygote couldn't be inside that cluster of cells after the change. But we're talking about something that could only work for the first few days after conception.<br /> <br /> Though I don't see anything that would break if you wanted to allow the child to survive via the mystic process of werewolf shapeshifting; you could add in some interesting possible implications of keeping a fetus in a spirit state like that for extended periods of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T12:22:58-07:00","id":461326,"title":"","content":"There is a sidebar about gender, sex, and pregnancy in the Children of Wolves section of the Storytelling chapter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gender is fluid and gender expression does not always relate to reproductive capability in the real world. For the supernatural creatures of the World of Darkness this is even more true. When discussing creatures like Wolf-Blooded and werewolves with powers like Luna\u2019s Embrace, gender should have no bearing on whether or not a character can become pregnant. The only thing that should stop a male character\u2019s pregnancy should be a player who doesn\u2019t want to tell that story. </div> </div> </div>So no, using Luna's Embrace does not, necessarily, terminate a pregnancy, unless that's the kind of story the player of the pregnant character wants to tell, and the rest of the group has expressly agreed that miscarriage is a subject they are ok with the game addressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-29-2015, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T13:12:53-07:00","id":461378,"title":"","content":"Spirits know no gender. The supernatural is not constrained by an artificial mortal binary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T13:15:15-07:00","id":461380,"title":"","content":"I'm sure you can find conceptual spirits of masculinity and femininity; in all cultural variations thereof.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:16:53-07:00","id":461449,"title":"","content":"I think part of the issue is that the social construct of gender, and the physical issue of biological parts are a bit at odds. WtF 2e definitely allows for far more gender fluidity than many games, but I think the question is more physical than not. A character that identifies as male, uses Luna's Embrace to have functional female reproductive organs and get pregnant doesn't have to stop identifying as male. But do they have to keep the uterus to keep the child?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:47:14-07:00","id":461506,"title":"","content":"Partial transformation. The werewolf becomes <i>mostly</i> male if they try to shift (back). Then when it's labour time that's when the girly parts become more persistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:47:44-07:00","id":461507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/461175-male-uratha-pregnancy?p=461449#post461449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the issue is that the social construct of gender, and the physical issue of biological parts are a bit at odds. WtF 2e definitely allows for far more gender fluidity than many games, but I think the question is more physical than not. A character that identifies as male, uses Luna's Embrace to have functional female reproductive organs and get pregnant doesn't have to stop identifying as male. But do they have to keep the uterus to keep the child?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's deliberately left up to each group to decide for themselves. Personally, I would never, ever kill a pregnant character's unborn child unless that was specifically where that player wanted the story to go and we had all as a group discussed it and agreed that miscarriage was an appropriate subject to bring up in the game. So in my games, a pregnant character could change sex with Luna's Embrace as much as they wanted and there would be no resulting complications. I'd just hand-wave the biological issues with spirit magic. Obviously what I would do is not what everyone would do, and different groups have to decide what is best for their own needs. I'm happy that the book leaves room for groups to make that decision, and doesn't say outright what is or isn't possible when the supernatural is involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:49:44-07:00","id":461509,"title":"","content":"In opposition to the &quot;spirit world doesnt know genders,&quot; uratha in fact do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:11:19-07:00","id":461582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/461175-male-uratha-pregnancy?p=461378#post461378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits know no gender. The supernatural is not constrained by an artificial mortal binary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits do breed, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:41:00-07:00","id":461605,"title":"","content":"Do they? I mean, like people? I was under the impression they just sort of grew over time in the reflection of whatever concept they express.<br /> <br /> but more importantly: do barnacle spirits barnacle off of other barnacle spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:54:05-07:00","id":461608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/461175-male-uratha-pregnancy?p=461605#post461605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they? I mean, like people? I was under the impression they just sort of grew over time in the reflection of whatever concept they express.<br /> <br /> but more importantly: do barnacle spirits barnacle off of other barnacle spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Father Wolf and Mother Moon (or Father Moon and Mother Wolf, if you prefer) are said to have mated to produce the Firstborn, and that one of them carried the Firstborn in pregnancy. I can see it happening with other spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:00:01-07:00","id":461616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/461175-male-uratha-pregnancy?p=461608#post461608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Father Wolf and Mother Moon (or Father Moon and Mother Wolf, if you prefer) are said to have mated to produce the Firstborn, and that one of them carried the Firstborn in pregnancy. I can see it happening with other spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always figured that was more poetic than literal. I don't know though, as far as I know there hasn't been much discussion on the specifics of spirit reproduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:07:50-07:00","id":461619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/461175-male-uratha-pregnancy?p=461608#post461608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Father Wolf and Mother Moon (or Father Moon and Mother Wolf, if you prefer) are said to have mated to produce the Firstborn, and that one of them carried the Firstborn in pregnancy. I can see it happening with other spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is, whether their &quot;mating&quot; and &quot;pregnancy&quot; are really all that equivalent to our material expectation of these terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:19:30-07:00","id":461623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/461175-male-uratha-pregnancy?p=461619#post461619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is, whether their &quot;mating&quot; and &quot;pregnancy&quot; are really all that equivalent to our material expectation of these terms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the legend goes that Luna, or now possibly Urfarah, took a human form to do it. Otherwise you're left with the lingering question of, 'Why did two spirits mating create a half-human half-spirit Uratha?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-29-2015, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":